  "live_records": {
    "q-126558": {
      "dom_id": "step-q126558",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14146138/assets/7264984a1c19c247c030feae04615bb0c46205ca70475db1240db964ad6007b2.png)\n\nSuppose that $F$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n{∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=10,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=-4,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=-2,\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}$ is oriented counterclockwise and ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are oriented clockwise, calculate the value of ${∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.$",
      "worked_solution": "To calculate the total circulation of a vector field over the boundary of a region containing holes, we add together the circulations over each *positively oriented* boundary.\n\nRemember that:\n\n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14146138/assets/0de833fcc39b6295418c1558cf1187774db7b4ada1d697f2dcac8c35858563df.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =10-4-2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
